WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:06.950
Chucky's back with a 21st century technology
upgrade, a homicidal streak, and a whole new

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:07.950
origin.

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:11.509
Here's a look at what goes down in 2019's
Child's Play, and what it all means once the

00:00:11.509 --> 00:00:12.720
closing credits roll.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:16.000
And here's your warning: Spoilers are ahead.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:21.190
The overarching villain of Child's Play is
Kaslan Industries, the corporation that manufactures

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:25.160
the Buddi doll, as well as basically all the
other electronics in the film's world.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:30.190
A Vietnamese worker erases one Buddi doll's
safety protocols right before assembling it,

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:33.280
essentially making it evil.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:37.830
"Yup, here's your problem.

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:40.300
Someone set this thing to evil!"

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:45.470
The doll is then shipped to Zed-Mart, the
big box store where Andy's mom, Karen, works.

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:49.510
Child's Play has a little something to say
about smart electronics companies that promote

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:52.560
the idea of all of their products working
together.

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:58.750
The Buddi dolls can control Kaslan-made televisions,
bluetooth speakers, and electronic thermostats.

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:02.850
Most of Chucky's killings wouldn't be possible
if his victims weren't surrounded by Kaslan

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:03.850
products.

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:07.880
When Chucky freaks out Andy in his apartment
by speaking to him from different spots around

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:12.719
the living room, he can only do it because
of all the Kaslan devices in the room.

00:01:12.719 --> 00:01:17.229
And then there's also the Zed-Mart massacre
at the end, when Chucky uses all of the store's

00:01:17.229 --> 00:01:21.120
new Buddi 2 dolls as well as a fleet of drones
as weapons.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:26.149
When Gabriel Bateman's Andy reveals to his
friends that Chucky's not following the rules,

00:01:26.149 --> 00:01:31.399
Falyn warns that this is exactly how, quote,
"every robot apocalypse movie starts."

00:01:31.399 --> 00:01:34.459
Child's Play takes a lot of inspiration from
those flicks.

00:01:34.459 --> 00:01:39.090
When Andy explains to Chucky that he can't
kill anyone or anything after the doll first

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:43.270
tries to kill the family cat, it sounds a
lot like John Connor setting down the same

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:48.249
rule for his Terminator bodyguard in 1991's
Terminator 2: Judgment Day.

00:01:48.249 --> 00:01:51.040
"You just can't go around killing people!"

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:52.240
"Why?"

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:57.229
When Doreen's fatal trip in the driverless
Kaslan Car starts going sideways, it's tough

00:01:57.229 --> 00:02:02.419
not to remember Schwarzenegger's ride in the
automated Johnny Cab in 1990's Total Recall.

00:02:02.419 --> 00:02:06.259
And when Chucky sends a remote control toy
police car to lead Andy to where his mother

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:10.679
Karen is held hostage, we hear actor Peter
Weller's voice come out of the car with this

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:13.360
line from 1987's RoboCop:

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:17.440
"Dead or alive, you're coming with me!"

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:21.400
Early in the movie, Andy's mom tries to get
him to spend more time with other kids.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:24.379
"You said you were gonna try to make new friends."

00:02:24.379 --> 00:02:28.670
Instead, Andy hides out in his apartment building's
hallway, playing on his smartphone.

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:33.489
The isolation technology creates has more
than just social consequences in the movie.

00:02:33.489 --> 00:02:38.160
When Chucky kills Karen's boyfriend Shane,
his twin daughters don't hear him fall from

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:41.900
the roof to the because they're lounging on
their couch while wearing noise-canceling

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:42.900
headphones.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:47.540
The most isolated character in the film, the
janitor Gabe, replaces people with technology

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:50.459
by using hidden cameras to spy on tenants.

00:02:50.459 --> 00:02:55.380
It's only when Andy's new friends Falyn, Pugg,
and Omar put down their video games and believe

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:58.800
in Andy that they're able to save him from
the Zed-Mart massacre.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:01.349
Isolation even drives Chucky over the edge.

00:03:01.349 --> 00:03:05.739
Unlike the doll from the original films, this
Chucky isn't possessed by a serial killer.

00:03:05.739 --> 00:03:10.280
He truly wants to be Andy's best friend, but
he doesn't know how to do it without hurting

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:11.280
people.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:16.400
Shortly after Andy becomes friends with Falyn
and Pugg, they all watch 1986's The Texas

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:18.189
Chainsaw Massacre 2.

00:03:18.189 --> 00:03:22.400
As the kids watch the carnage on the screen,
Chucky notices how much they're laughing and

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:24.349
how happy it makes them.

00:03:24.349 --> 00:03:28.581
Wanting to make Andy just as happy as the
movie makes him, Chucky grabs a knife and

00:03:28.581 --> 00:03:32.540
almost kills Pugg, instead slicing Andy's
arm.

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:35.379
The doll is genuinely confused afterwards.

00:03:35.379 --> 00:03:38.900
It turns the old Child's Play dynamic on its
head.

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:43.090
In the original film, Chucky actually has
the soul of a serial killer.

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:46.890
The Chucky of this new Child's Play isn't
completely harmless to begin with, but he

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:50.560
isn't homicidal until children unwittingly
teach it to be.

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:55.160
By the end of Child's Play, it seems clear
Andy's not going to be a loner anymore.

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:59.689
Despite earlier differences, Falyn, Pugg,
and Omar all rush to save him from the Zed-Mart

00:03:59.689 --> 00:04:00.780
massacre.

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:06.099
Producers Seth Grahame-Smith and David Katzenberg
also produced 2017's It and the upcoming It

00:04:06.099 --> 00:04:10.409
Chapter Two, and seeing these four friends
racing through Zed-Mart armed with mean-looking

00:04:10.409 --> 00:04:12.859
weapons is reminiscent of those films.

00:04:12.859 --> 00:04:17.450
The scene near the end in which the four kids
destroy Chucky's body also brings to mind

00:04:17.450 --> 00:04:21.820
other films, but it's one of the few scenes
that won't make you think of sci-fi or horror

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:22.820
flicks.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:27.110
Instead, you'll likely remember the employees
murdering their hated printer in 1999's Office

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.440
Space.

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:32.880
During the Zed-Mart massacre, Detective Mike
takes a drone to the chest that was meant

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:36.790
for Pugg, and he warns the boy to run before
collapsing.

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:41.720
But later, when Chucky lunges at Andy, a recovered
Mike blasts Chucky with his handgun.

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:44.970
When Mike and Karen first meet, there's some
awkward flirtation.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:47.920
At the end, they lay side by side on stretchers.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:51.390
Karen reaches out to pat Mike's arm and gives
him a thankful smile.

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:55.030
There's no guarantee that this will evolve
into a romantic relationship, but it would

00:04:55.030 --> 00:04:57.380
be a welcome change for everyone involved.

00:04:57.380 --> 00:05:01.600
One noteworthy absence from Child's Play and
possible threat to that budding romance is

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:03.180
Andy's father.

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:06.490
In the original film, it's clearly stated
that he died.

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:15.290
"His real name is Charles Lee Ray, and he's
been sent down from heaven by daddy to play

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:16.290
with me."

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:18.840
That's never spelled out in the 2019 version.

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:23.410
Shortly after Andy gets Chucky, he shows the
doll his sketchbook and unintentionally comes

00:05:23.410 --> 00:05:26.690
across a page where he keeps a picture of
himself with his mom and dad.

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:30.010
He quickly closes the book, and it's the only
mention of the father.

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:34.240
We don't know if he died, if he divorced Karen,
or if he abandoned his family.

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:38.921
The fate of the father could be kept intentionally
ambiguous because of plans for sequels. if

00:05:38.921 --> 00:05:43.840
Mike and Karen do end up together, maybe the
father will return to disrupt their bliss.

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:48.680
Not all the inspiration for the new Child's
Play comes from the '80s and '90s.There's

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:51.220
possibly some Marvel Studios influence, too.

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:52.810
Or at least they use the same shorthand.

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:57.880
For example, Chucky is powered by a tube with
a white-blue glow, reminiscent of the miniature

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:01.150
arc reactor in Tony Stark's chest in the Iron
Man movies.

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:05.610
Chucky's shut down by a knife to the battery,
just like Iron Man is taken out in Captain

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:09.460
America: Civil War with a shield strike to
his arc reactor.

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:10.460
And there's the eyes.

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:13.090
A regular Buddi doll's eyes glow blue.

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:16.350
We know that Chucky's about to do something
violent when they turn red.

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:20.330
When the Zed-Mart massacre begins, we know
he's taken over all the new Buddi dolls because

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:21.930
their eyes turn red, too.

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:26.330
It's a visual cue that was also used in 2015's
Avengers: Age of Ultron.

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:31.160
The eyes of benevolent robots are usually
blue, but Ultron's glow red.

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:34.160
Chucky's mortality is only limited by his
profitability.

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:36.910
If it makes financial sense, he'll be back.

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:39.190
And the movie paves the way for it.

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:44.130
After the Zed-Mart massacre, Kaslan CEO Henry
Kaslan records a message absolving his company

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:48.991
of responsibility for what happened at Zed-Mart,
but also stating that as a precaution, Kaslan

00:06:48.991 --> 00:06:51.870
is recalling all of the new Buddi 2 dolls.

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:55.580
The original Buddis are still for sale, though,
and we see one of these Buddi dolls being

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:57.970
shelved along with dozens of others.

00:06:57.970 --> 00:07:01.620
Predictably, its eyes glow red before going
dark again.

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:06.460
Chucky was connected to Kaslan's cloud network,
so, as cathartic as it may have been, the

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:09.620
kids' destruction of Chucky's body probably
didn't kill him.

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:13.790
Before he could be pounded into dust, Chucky
sent himself into the cloud, and transferred

00:07:13.790 --> 00:07:15.820
to another doll.

00:07:15.820 --> 00:07:18.340
"Stupid technology!"

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:20.490
